\section{Journal Selection}

Apeiron-CM's scientific scope spans general relativity, quantum-field 
gradient dynamics, magnetohydrodynamics, distributed computation, and 
high-order numerical integration. The following journals are identified 
as optimal publication targets based on domain alignment and LaTeX 
submission compatibility.

\subsection{Physical Review D (APS)}
\textbf{Domain:} General relativity, cosmology, quantum fields, numerical relativity. \\
\textbf{Rationale:} Apeiron-CM's centimeter-scale GR engine, causal 
firewall, and stress-energy conservation proofs align directly with PRD's 
focus on relativistic physics. \\
\textbf{Submission Format:} LaTeX (REVTeX 4.2).

\subsection{Journal of Computational Physics (Elsevier)}
\textbf{Domain:} High-order integrators, multi-physics solvers, 
distributed numerical computation. \\
\textbf{Rationale:} The 14th-order Gauss-Legendre integrator, Liouville 
invariance validation, and stress-test matrix (ST-01 through ST-05) 
represent core contributions to computational physics. \\
\textbf{Submission Format:} LaTeX.

\subsection{Classical and Quantum Gravity (IOP)}
\textbf{Domain:} Numerical relativity, spacetime modeling, causal 
structure enforcement. \\
\textbf{Rationale:} Apeiron-CM's light-cone compliance and causal 
firewall mechanisms provide novel contributions to relativistic 
simulation methodology. \\
\textbf{Submission Format:} LaTeX.

\subsection{Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society (MNRAS)}
\textbf{Domain:} Cosmological simulation engines, astrophysical 
turbulence, distributed computation in cosmology. \\
\textbf{Rationale:} The engine's MHD turbulence fidelity, Kolmogorov 
spectral alignment, and distributed mesh execution make it suitable for 
computational astrophysics. \\
\textbf{Submission Format:} LaTeX.

\subsection{SIAM Journal on Scientific Computing}
\textbf{Domain:} Numerical analysis, stability proofs, high-performance 
computing architectures. \\
\textbf{Rationale:} Apeiron-CM's invariant preservation, error-scaling 
curves, and distributed stress resilience match SIAM's standards for 
scientific computing. \\
\textbf{Submission Format:} LaTeX.

\subsection{IEEE Transactions on Parallel and Distributed Systems}
\textbf{Domain:} RDMA fabrics, fault-tolerant distributed computation, 
synchronization under load. \\
\textbf{Rationale:} The engine's RDMA saturation tolerance, packet-loss 
recovery, and causal firewall represent significant contributions to 
distributed systems research. \\
\textbf{Submission Format:} LaTeX.